# Vendors live in the guest

The factory builds Go from vendor docs. That guest owns how to connect, send, and receive (URLs, form vs JSON, display names, which conversations are visible).

The host must not implement Slack, Telegram, Discord, WhatsApp, or other vendor HTTP — no form encoders, users.info, auth.test, or conversation-list filters in Structure, HostUI, or DerrickBackend.

Host work: forward `http.request` as declared, attach secrets, persist `result.emit`, render HostUI.

Allowed: `contracts/vendors/*.json` as builder input; Slack MCP harnesses as tests. Not allowed: host runtime that speaks a vendor.

If David asks for host-side vendor protocol code, warn first.
